1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:02,399
The balloon!

2
00:00:03,399 --> 00:00:05,639
No way! You'll miss for sure!

3
00:00:06,160 --> 00:00:07,160
No problem!

4
00:00:12,759 --> 00:00:14,439
Anybody can do that!

5
00:00:14,679 --> 00:00:18,519
But I bet you can't do it if you tried bouncing the ball off the floor first!

6
00:00:18,719 --> 00:00:19,879
Just look!

7
00:00:22,839 --> 00:00:24,800
Oh, what are my parents going to do to me?

8
00:00:25,320 --> 00:00:26,879
Maybe we should call Simka.

9
00:00:27,080 --> 00:00:28,120
Simka!

10
00:00:28,120 --> 00:00:31,359
And what's Simka going to do to us when she sees this?

11
00:00:33,320 --> 00:00:36,079
So, got yourself in trouble, huh?

12
00:00:37,160 --> 00:00:39,480
You shouldn't be playing with a ball inside.

13
00:00:39,560 --> 00:00:41,560
And now we have your lamp to fix!

14
00:00:41,880 --> 00:00:42,880
But how?

15
00:00:43,120 --> 00:00:45,600
Only my dad can reach all the way up there!

16
00:00:45,920 --> 00:00:47,400
Why just your dad?

17
00:00:47,560 --> 00:00:49,920
You have a hot air balloon over there!

18
00:00:50,400 --> 00:00:53,120
That doesn't fly. It's just a toy, see?

19
00:00:53,480 --> 00:00:55,320
Well, it might be just a toy to you,

20
00:00:55,320 --> 00:00:58,399
but for us Fixies, it's absolutely real!

21
00:01:00,799 --> 00:01:04,840
If an object is lighter than water, it floats up to the surface.

22
00:01:05,239 --> 00:01:09,200
And in the same way, if something is lighter than air, it floats upward.

23
00:01:09,719 --> 00:01:12,640
Did you know that hot air is lighter than cold air?

24
00:01:12,799 --> 00:01:13,760
Well, it is!

25
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:17,960
And that means if you warm up the air in a balloon, it will float up!

26
00:01:18,400 --> 00:01:22,799
Hot air balloons use special gas burners to heat up the air inside of them

27
00:01:22,879 --> 00:01:24,280
so they will get lighter.

28
00:01:24,879 --> 00:01:29,159
And the bigger the balloon, the more people it can take up into the air.

29
00:01:31,480 --> 00:01:34,480
I know what you're saying, but where do we get a burner?

30
00:01:34,840 --> 00:01:37,159
You think Fixies don't have their own burners?

31
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:39,240
Sure we've got them!

32
00:01:39,359 --> 00:01:42,319
Bring it down here and I'll go talk to our parents.

33
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:45,719
No, no and no!

34
00:01:45,920 --> 00:01:49,000
The human child must never see us!

35
00:01:49,359 --> 00:01:50,640
Listen now, Simka.

36
00:01:50,760 --> 00:01:53,960
We already don't approve of him seeing you and Nolik.

37
00:01:54,280 --> 00:01:55,519
He won't look!

38
00:01:55,799 --> 00:01:57,239
Papus, please!

39
00:01:57,560 --> 00:02:02,079
You're the one who told us how you dreamed of flying since you trained to go into space?

40
00:02:02,760 --> 00:02:03,519
Yeah.

41
00:02:03,760 --> 00:02:07,439
For two years I waited on standby, but I never went up.

42
00:02:08,479 --> 00:02:11,240
And you've never flown on a hot air balloon either, Honey.

43
00:02:11,400 --> 00:02:13,000
So let's call it a deal!

44
00:02:15,680 --> 00:02:16,960
I talked them into it.

45
00:02:17,120 --> 00:02:19,520
There's just one condition – you can't watch.

46
00:02:20,240 --> 00:02:21,080
OK.

47
00:02:21,080 --> 00:02:25,200
You can come in now.

48
00:02:31,400 --> 00:02:33,300
Now prepare the burner.

49
00:02:33,960 --> 00:02:35,200
Coming right up.

50
00:02:36,740 --> 00:02:38,260
Permission for takeoff?

51
00:02:38,540 --> 00:02:39,740
Permission is granted.

52
00:02:41,880 --> 00:02:43,800
And off we go!

53
00:02:44,260 --> 00:02:46,500
Hooray! It's flying!

54
00:02:47,460 --> 00:02:49,560
Don't you peek. Turn around.

55
00:02:49,560 --> 00:02:51,560
Oh, it was an accident!

56
00:03:00,560 --> 00:03:02,560
I'm going to evaluate the damage!

57
00:03:02,560 --> 00:03:04,560
Maintaining proper altitude!

58
00:03:10,560 --> 00:03:12,560
So, they've reached the spot!

59
00:03:12,560 --> 00:03:14,560
Air balloons are really awesome!

60
00:03:14,560 --> 00:03:17,560
I wonder who figured out how to do that?

61
00:03:17,560 --> 00:03:19,560
It was the Montgolfiers.

62
00:03:21,560 --> 00:03:24,560
The hot air balloon was invented in the 18th century

63
00:03:24,560 --> 00:03:27,560
by the Montgolfier brothers from France.

64
00:03:27,560 --> 00:03:29,560
In those days there were no gas burners,

65
00:03:29,560 --> 00:03:33,560
so they heated the air inside the balloon by burning straw.

66
00:03:34,560 --> 00:03:37,560
At first there were no passengers on their balloon,

67
00:03:37,560 --> 00:03:39,560
not counting the Fixies, of course.

68
00:03:39,560 --> 00:03:42,560
I mean, how else could a balloon get up in the air without them?

69
00:03:43,560 --> 00:03:45,560
Unfortunately, the names of the first Fixies

70
00:03:45,560 --> 00:03:49,400
who took that flight were not recorded in the annals of history.

71
00:03:49,759 --> 00:03:53,159
Following the Fixies' flight, the next passengers were animals –

72
00:03:53,240 --> 00:03:55,840
a ram, a rooster, and a duck.

73
00:03:56,080 --> 00:04:01,240
And it was not until those three safely landed after flying a full four kilometers

74
00:04:01,319 --> 00:04:05,120
that humans dared to fly in hot air balloons themselves.

75
00:04:05,319 --> 00:04:09,640
Ever since their invention, hot air balloons have also gone by another name –

76
00:04:09,719 --> 00:04:11,400
Montgolfiers!

77
00:04:15,560 --> 00:04:22,560
All right! Simka, please let your parents know that I'm so very thankful.

78
00:04:22,560 --> 00:04:25,560
OK. By the way, now you can turn around.

79
00:04:28,560 --> 00:04:31,560
You know, Simka, let's fly the balloon just like them.

80
00:04:39,560 --> 00:04:44,360
There's no way, Nolik. We would need to use the burner, and kids aren't allowed to play with fire.

81
00:04:44,720 --> 00:04:45,920
I'll give you a ride.

82
00:04:46,160 --> 00:04:50,280
Look, I still need to put it back up on the shelf, so climb in and let's do it!

83
00:04:54,360 --> 00:04:57,840
Oh yeah! This is great, Simka!

84
00:04:58,079 --> 00:05:02,199
Look at us! We're flying just like the Montgolfier brothers!

85
00:05:02,519 --> 00:05:04,079
What do you mean like brothers?

86
00:05:04,160 --> 00:05:08,000
OK then, like brother and sister Montgolfier!

